00:32:03.320 --> 00:32:04.503
need to be studied.

588
00:32:05.400 --> 00:32:08.380
How many of the decisions that you made against advice

589
00:32:08.380 --> 00:32:11.030
over the last X amount of time,

590
00:32:11.030 --> 00:32:14.820
you talked about we can do more in a year,

591
00:32:14.820 --> 00:32:18.677
or, no, we can do less in a year, but more than a decade,

592
00:32:18.677 --> 00:32:21.890
how many of the decisions that we've acted upon

593
00:32:21.890 --> 00:32:24.150
against advice have turned out?

594
00:32:24.150 --> 00:32:27.750
Is it greater than 50% or less than 50%?

595
00:32:27.750 --> 00:32:30.794
And start coming up with some conclusions

596
00:32:30.794 --> 00:32:32.780
based on real data.

597
00:32:32.780 --> 00:32:35.740
Another way to parse this or look at it,

598
00:32:35.740 --> 00:32:39.770
again, I always go back to the addiction recovery,

599
00:32:39.770 --> 00:32:41.380
I've lens on these things.

600
00:32:41.380 --> 00:32:42.213
It's a beautiful.

601
00:32:42.213 --> 00:32:46.760
One of the things that I've learned is evaluating

602
00:32:46.760 --> 00:32:50.503
these decisions or these impulses or these intuitions

603
00:32:50.503 --> 00:32:55.503
through a calculus of what hole am I trying to fill.

604
00:32:56.770 --> 00:33:00.251
So if I have this notion that pops into my head,

605
00:33:00.251 --> 00:33:04.904
I am feeling very hungry.

606
00:33:04.904 --> 00:33:09.150
I'm protein starved, I must go to McDonald's.

607
00:33:09.150 --> 00:33:11.879
McDonald's is the solution to my problem.

608
00:33:11.879 --> 00:33:13.780
That is my instinct,

609
00:33:13.780 --> 00:33:16.610
that is my gut, it's telling me

610
00:33:16.610 --> 00:33:19.401
that's how I'm gonna solve this hunger that I have.

611
00:33:19.401 --> 00:33:22.710
Well, let's deconstruct that a little bit.

612
00:33:22.710 --> 00:33:24.455
Are you truly protein deficient?

613
00:33:24.455 --> 00:33:26.860
What's driving this hunger?

614
00:33:26.860 --> 00:33:29.900
And what is the emotional discomfort

615
00:33:29.900 --> 00:33:31.175
that you're feeling right now

616
00:33:31.175 --> 00:33:35.820
that your unconscious mind is telling you

617
00:33:35.820 --> 00:33:40.670
will be resolved by putting a gigantic amount of calories

618
00:33:41.870 --> 00:33:45.170
into your gut as quickly as possible?

619
00:33:45.170 --> 00:33:47.976
That will essentially sedate you.

620
00:33:47.976 --> 00:33:52.976
It's an addictive response to an emotional discomfort

621
00:33:53.250 --> 00:33:55.810
that's driving that decision.

622
00:33:55.810 --> 00:34:00.810
Thus, it is less intuition and it is more impulse,

623
00:34:01.420 --> 00:34:06.420
an impulse driven by an unconscious emotional need.

624
00:34:07.180 --> 00:34:09.920
Well, you said the word sedation,

625
00:34:09.920 --> 00:34:14.640
because the unconscious emotional need will remain

626
00:34:14.640 --> 00:34:19.120
once that food is digested and wears off.

627
00:34:19.120 --> 00:34:21.300
Well, you will be sedated for a moment.

628
00:34:21.300 --> 00:34:23.370
You will be sedated so that you won't experience the need.

629
00:34:23.370 --> 00:34:25.900
And then your emotional dis-ease will return.

630
00:34:25.900 --> 00:34:27.150
Exactly.

631
00:34:27.150 --> 00:34:32.150
And what is a more appropriate view in that moment

632
00:34:32.450 --> 00:34:36.870
is to go, okay, my impulse is this.

633
00:34:36.870 --> 00:34:41.870
And by asking yourself, what hole am I trying to fill,

634
00:34:42.948 --> 00:34:45.591
it's got many layers, doesn't it?

635
00:34:45.591 --> 00:34:48.420
And there's many different aspects to the hole

636
00:34:49.310 --> 00:34:50.629
that is being filled here.

637
00:34:50.629 --> 00:34:55.629
And maybe if we just withheld some of the consumption

638
00:34:56.119 --> 00:34:59.740
and spend a little more time in the evaluation,

639
00:34:59.740 --> 00:35:03.140
we might realize something that could be reapplied

640
00:35:03.140 --> 00:35:06.540
over and over and over again successfully

641
00:35:06.540 --> 00:35:08.969
that ultimately ends up changing

642
00:35:08.969 --> 00:35:11.574
the fact that that even comes up.

643
00:35:11.574 --> 00:35:14.694
That we may never have to ultimately

644
00:35:14.694 --> 00:35:19.694
face that same challenge, that same emotional need,

645
00:35:21.060 --> 00:35:24.060
that same hole that needs to be filled.

646
00:35:24.060 --> 00:35:25.255
Yeah.

647
00:35:25.255 --> 00:35:28.420
If you're constantly reaching out to fill the hole

648
00:35:28.420 --> 00:35:29.890
and doing it impulsively

649
00:35:29.890 --> 00:35:34.110
without any kind of higher cognizance of what's going on,

